  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for Water and Sanitation in India (SUWASI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  . ..Using FY 2022 funds, USAID will continue its support to the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs (MOHUA) as well as selected State and Municipal governments for the implementation of the Swachh Bharat Mission Urban (SBM-U) at the national, state and city levels. The project management unit (PMU), based in the MOHUA, is primarily engaged in providing technical assistance related to national level guidelines, protocols and advisories, and initiatives. The PMU is supporting cities to progress beyond Open Defecation Free (ODF) status and move towards achieving ODF+, ODF++ and Water+ certification. Specifically, in the coming year, the activity will focus, among other things, on: (i) policies, standards, practices, and financial viability related to wastewater and fecal sludge treatment and reuse; (ii) helping to establish centers of excellence for sustainable skilling and capacity building; (iii) promoting private sector engagement, particularly through innovative financial frameworks; (iv) rejuvenation of water bodies and source sustainability; and (v) identifying and promoting technology innovations and partnerships with start-ups in the water and wastewater sector... ..This implementing mechanism contributes to the Safe Latrines... .</narrative>
  </description>
